{"slug": "holy-bean-soup", "nyt_id": 1114, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1114-holy-bean-soup", "name": "Holy Bean Soup", "author": "Molly O’Neill", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "8 servings", "min": 8, "max": 8, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 195, "raw": {"total": "3 hours 15 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 tablespoons butter", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "butter", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 carrots", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "carrots", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 stalks celery", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "stalk", "item": "celery", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 large onion", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large onion", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "4 cloves garlic", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 ½ tablespoons curry powder", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "curry powder", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 pound white beans, dried", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "white beans", "preparation": "dried", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "Salt and freshly ground black pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and freshly ground black pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Melt the butter in a large soup pot over medium heat. Put the carrots, celery, onion and garlic in a food processor and process until smooth but still chunky."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Transfer to the pot and cook, stirring for 5 minutes. Add half the curry, stir and cook until the vegetables are nearly soft, about 5 more minutes."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Add the beans and gallon cold water. Bring to a boil and simmer for 3 hours, adding more water to keep the beans covered by 1 inch. Season with salt and pepper to taste and add the remaining curry powder to taste. Serve with crusty bread."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 236.3, "protein_g": 14.0, "carbohydrates_g": 39.1, "fat_g": 3.6, "saturated_fat_g": 2.0, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 7.6, "sodium_mg": 249.4, "fiber_g": 10.3, "sugar_g": 2.9, "unsaturated_fat_g": 1.4, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner", "lunch"], "occasion": [], "other": ["boil", "curry powder", "great leftovers", "one pot", "saute", "soup", "white bean"]}, "images": [], "rating": null, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1997-12-07", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:01:06.482380+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "honey-peaches-and-cream-pudding", "nyt_id": 785954707, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/785954707-honey-peaches-and-cream-pudding", "name": "Honey Peaches and Cream Pudding", "author": "Carolina Gelen", "description": "Following the structure of a classic banana pudding, this honeyed peach pudding is here to make the most out of the peach season and celebrate the orange-fleshed juicy fruit. With layers of honey-sweetened peaches, silky vanilla pudding, freshly whipped cream, and crisp vanilla wafers to soak up the spiced peach juices, it’s easy to see how this dessert tastes like summer on a plate. Great for working through those overripe peaches on your counter in the middle of summer, this recipe uses three pounds of them, ensuring each scoop has a tender peach to bite into. While the recipe doesn’t call for it, peeling the peaches yields a silkier texture if you have a chance to tackle that process.", "servings": {"text": "12-16 servings", "min": 12, "max": 16, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 10, "cook_minutes": 160, "total_minutes": 170, "raw": {"total": "50 min, plus 2 hr chilling", "prep": "PT0H10M", "cook": "PT2H40M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "3 pounds ripe peaches (10 to 12 medium peaches)", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "ripe peaches (10 to 12 medium peaches)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "¼ cup honey", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "honey", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 tablespoons lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 teaspoons vanilla extract", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "vanilla extract", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 tablespoon orange blossom water, optional", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "orange blossom water", "preparation": null, "optional": true}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 teaspoon ground cardamom", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground cardamom", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ teaspoon kosher salt, such as Diamond Crystal", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "kosher salt", "preparation": "such as Diamond Crystal", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "2 cups whole milk", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "whole milk", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 (3.4-ounce) packet instant vanilla pudding mix (or make your own; see Tip)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "(3.4-ounce) packet instant vanilla pudding mix (or make your own; see tip)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "2 tablespoons honey", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "honey", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "2 teaspoons vanilla extract", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "vanilla extract", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "½ teaspoon kosher salt, such as Diamond Crystal", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "kosher salt", "preparation": "such as Diamond Crystal", "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "1 ½ cups heavy cream", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "heavy cream", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "1 (11-ounce) package vanilla wafer cookies", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "(11-ounce) package vanilla wafer cookies", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "2 cups heavy cream", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "heavy cream", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "¼ cup honey, plus more for topping", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "honey", "preparation": "plus more for topping", "optional": false}, {"position": 17, "raw": "1 ½ teaspoons ground cardamom", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground cardamom", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 18, "raw": "¼ teaspoon kosher salt, such as Diamond Crystal", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "kosher salt", "preparation": "such as Diamond Crystal", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Prepare the peaches: Set aside 2 whole peaches and 12 vanilla wafers for the topping. Cut the remaining peaches into bite-sized chunks. In a medium bowl, toss together the peaches, honey, lemon juice, vanilla, orange blossom water (if using), cardamom and salt and set aside to macerate."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Make the pudding: In a medium bowl, whisk together the milk, instant pudding mix, honey, vanilla and salt. Set aside in the fridge for 5 minutes. In a large bowl, using a hand mixer or a stand mixer with the whisk attachment, whip the heavy cream to stiff peaks. Add the pudding to the whipped cream and gently fold until combined. (The peaches and the pudding can be prepped up to 2 days ahead; store them separately in the refrigerator until ready to assemble.)"}, {"position": 3, "text": "In a 9-by-13-inch casserole dish, spread half of the pudding, then top with half of the vanilla wafers in an even layer. Drizzle about 3 tablespoons of the liquid from the macerated peaches over the wafers (save any remaining peach syrup to use in fizzy iced drinks). Using a slotted spoon, scoop half of the peaches and layer on top of the wafers. Repeat one more time, using the remaining pudding, wafers and sliced peaches."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Cover and chill the assembled pudding in the fridge for at least 3 hours (or up to 1 day.)"}, {"position": 5, "text": "Before serving (or up to 2 days in advance), make the topping: In a medium bowl, whip the heavy cream to stiff peaks. Add the honey, cardamom and salt and gently stir to combine."}, {"position": 6, "text": "When ready to serve, dollop the whipped cream on the pudding, swirling it around with the back of a spoon until it reaches the sides of the bowl. Garnish with the reserved vanilla wafers, then cut the reserved peaches into small wedges and arrange on top. Finish with a drizzle of honey."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 439.7, "protein_g": 4.9, "carbohydrates_g": 48.2, "fat_g": 26.6, "saturated_fat_g": 15.3, "trans_fat_g": 0.9, "cholesterol_mg": 72.7, "sodium_mg": 368.8, "fiber_g": 2.0, "sugar_g": 38.5, "unsaturated_fat_g": 9.4, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["southern inspired"], "diet": ["peanut-free", "tree nut-free", "soy-free", "fish-free", "shellfish-free", "pork-free", "sesame-free", "alcohol-free", "vegetarian", "pescatarian"], "course": ["dessert"], "meal": [], "occasion": ["party"], "other": ["peach", "honey", "heavy cream", "cardamom", "custards and puddings", "parfaits and trifles", "no cook", "make-ahead", "milk", "summer", "creator", "plan-ahead"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/08/07/multimedia/CG-Honey-Peaches-and-Cream-Pudding-1-jzmw/CG-Honey-Peaches-and-Cream-Pudding-1-jzmw-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 57}, "video_url": "https://www.nytimes.com/video/embedded/dining/100000011071861/honey-peaches-and-cream-pudding.html", "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2026-08-06", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T2